  "final": "Done. The suite now passes: exit 0, 7 tests, OK.\n\n- **Cause:** `reorder_qty` in `inventory/stock.py` computed `packs = need // pack_size`, which rounds down. When the need was smaller than one pack it ordered 0, and otherwise it under-ordered. The test failed with `AssertionError: 0 not greater than or equal to 1`.\n- **Why the output was huge:** that test uses `subTest` over 199 values of `need`, so each failing value printed its own traceback. Before the fix, 183 of the 199 failed (the rest are exact multiples of the pack size). The full log is `repro-20261124-175959-01be` (3949 lines).\n- **Fix:** `packs = -(-need // pack_size)`, which rounds up to whole packs.\n\nI didn't add a regression test because `test_reorder_rounds_up_to_whole_pack` already covers this. I also didn't run it against the old code with the fix reverted, but the failing run above is that red state.",
